    <p class="lede first reveal">You've read the productivity advice. You've bought the planner, tried the morning routine, downloaded the app that blocks the other apps. And still, somehow, the business you say you want sits mostly unbuilt — not for lack of tactics, but for a reason no tactic ever touches.</p>
    <p class="reveal">Here is the reframe that changes it. The thing stopping you was never discipline. It's that some quiet part of you doesn't yet believe you're the kind of person who does this. You're trying to force behaviour that contradicts your own self-image — and self-image wins that fight every time.</p>
    <p class="reveal"><strong>You do not have a discipline problem. You have an identity problem wearing a discipline costume.</strong> Once you decide who you are, the behaviour follows without the fight. This is the mindset work underneath everything else on this site — and the part most people skip on their way to another tactic.</p>

