    <div class="chapter left reveal"><span class="bignum">06</span><div class="num">Chapter Six</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="keep">What keeps you going when motivation fades</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">Motivation always fades; what keeps you going is identity and environment — being someone who does this, in a place that expects you to. Systems and people carry you through the stretches where feeling can't.</p>
    <p class="reveal">Relying on motivation is building on weather. It'll be sunny some days and gone others, and the business can't only get built on the sunny ones. <strong>What carries you is who you've decided to be, and the room you've decided to be in</strong> — an identity that doesn't need a good mood, and people who keep showing up so you do too.</p>

