    <div class="chapter reveal"><div class="num">Answered</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="faq">Frequently asked</h2></div>
    <h3 class="reveal">How do I stay disciplined enough to build a business?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">By stopping the reliance on discipline. Most consistency problems are identity problems — you struggle to act like someone you don't yet believe you are. Decide you're the kind of person who builds and finishes things, and the behaviour stops needing to be forced.</p>
    <h3 class="reveal">What is the Creator to CEO shift?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">It's the move from seeing yourself as someone who makes things to someone who runs a business — from "what should I make?" to "what does this business need me to decide?" It changes what you build and how you spend your time, and it's a mindset change before it's a practical one.</p>
    <h3 class="reveal">How do I start when I never feel ready?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">You start before the feeling arrives, because readiness comes from action, not before it. Start small and imperfectly; the confidence you're waiting for is built by the very thing you're avoiding. Naming your intention out loud to others makes the first step far easier to take.</p>

